# stackguardian_workflow_git (Resource)

{{ .Description | trimspace }}

## When to use this instead of `stackguardian_workflow_from_template`

Use `stackguardian_workflow_git` when the IaC lives in a repository you control and you want the
workflow defined in one place. Use [`stackguardian_workflow_from_template`](https://registry.terraform.io/providers/StackGuardian/stackguardian/latest/docs/resources/workflow_from_template)
when several workflows should share a definition and inherit updates from a published revision.

## Choosing the `id`

Unlike most resources, `id` is **required** — you choose the workflow's ID rather than the server
assigning one. Changing it replaces the workflow.

## VCS triggers

`vcs_triggers` registers a webhook with your VCS provider, so it requires the repository to be
reachable: set `vcs_config.iac_vcs_config.custom_source.config.is_private` to `true` and point
`auth` at a `stackguardian_connector`.

Two behaviours are worth knowing before you enable it:

- **If trigger registration fails during create, the workflow is deleted.** The provider removes
  the workflow it just created rather than leaving one behind with no working triggers, and the
  apply fails. Fix the connector or repository access and apply again.
- **Removing the `vcs_triggers` block does not unregister existing webhooks.** The provider only
  sends trigger configuration when the block is present, so webhooks registered by an earlier
  apply remain in place. Remove them in the VCS provider, or in the StackGuardian UI.

